---
/**
 * /affiliate-disclosure/ — Affiliate Disclosure.
 *
 * THE CENTRAL FACT: no affiliate programme is configured. The project was
 * searched for affiliate networks, tracking identifiers, programme names,
 * commission terms and product URLs — none exists. `site.ts` still lists
 * "final affiliate program + product URLs" as unresolved, the article
 * collection is empty, and `getPublishedArticles()` returns nothing, so there
 * is not a single affiliate link on this website today.
 *
 * ON AMAZON SPECIFICALLY: Amazon appears in the project brief only as a DESIGN
 * CONSTRAINT — "must not feel like an Amazon affiliate site" — and in the
 * unresolved-inputs list. That is not a configured relationship, and there is
 * no approved Associates disclosure wording anywhere in the project. So Amazon
 * is not named as a partner here and no programme-specific or required-form
 * wording is reproduced. Inventing a tracking ID or quoting a programme's
 * mandated sentence without being in that programme would be a false statement
 * about a commercial relationship.
 *
 * The page therefore describes the intended model honestly, in the future
 * tense, and says plainly that nothing is live yet. It is written to be
 * accurate now AND to need only a small, obvious edit once a programme exists.
 *
 * This is website copy, not legal advice, and no compliance claim is made.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalPage from '../components/page/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { siteFacts } from '../config/legal';

/** Verified: no programme configured, nothing published. */
const { affiliateProgramConfigured, affiliateLinksPublished } = siteFacts;
const anyAffiliateActivity = affiliateProgramConfigured || affiliateLinksPublished;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure"
  description="How affiliate links work on SpaceWise Living, and their current status."
  bare
>
  <LegalPage
    eyebrow="Legal / Affiliate Disclosure"
    title="Affiliate Disclosure"
    intro={`${site.name} is intended to use affiliate links in some of its content. This page explains what that means, and what is actually in place today.`}
    contactHeading="Questions"
    contactIntro="If you have a question about affiliate links on this site, you can get in touch once a contact route is available."
  >
    {
      !anyAffiliateActivity && (
        <>
          <h2>Current status</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>
              There are no affiliate links on this website at the moment.
            </strong>{' '}
            No affiliate programme has been set up, and no articles have been
            published yet. Nothing on this site currently earns a commission.
          </p>
          <p>
            This page is published in advance so the arrangement is clear before
            the first such link ever appears. It will be updated to name the
            programmes actually in use when that happens.
          </p>
        </>
      )
    }

    <h2>How affiliate links work</h2>
    <p>
      An affiliate link is an ordinary link to a retailer that also tells that
      retailer you arrived from here. If you buy something after following one,
      the retailer may pay a small commission to the referring site.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where {site.name} uses them, only <em>some</em> links in <em>some</em>{' '}
      content will be affiliate links. Plenty of links — to reference material,
      to makers, or simply to something worth looking at — earn nothing at all.
    </p>

    <h2>Your price does not increase</h2>
    <p>
      An affiliate commission is paid by the retailer out of a sale that has
      already happened. Following an affiliate link does not add anything to
      what you pay, and it does not change the price you are shown.
    </p>

    <h2>How things are chosen to feature</h2>
    <p>
      Recommendations here are editorial judgements about what tends to help
      with a specific small-space problem — whether something suits an awkward
      corner, a shallow cabinet or a shared room.
    </p>
    <p>
      To be straightforward about it: these are not hands-on product reviews.
      Nothing on this site should be read as a claim that an item has been
      bought, tested, measured or lived with, and no performance, durability or
      safety testing is implied. Check the dimensions and the retailer's own
      details against your own space before buying anything.
    </p>

    <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
    <p>
      Affiliate relationships do not change the purpose of the site: to publish
      practical small-space organization ideas and useful recommendations. The
      problem comes first and the product second — the aim is that an article is
      worth reading even if you buy nothing at all.
    </p>

    <h2>Identifying affiliate content</h2>
    <p>
      Where affiliate links are used, they will be disclosed on the page that
      contains them, near the recommendation rather than buried at the bottom,
      so you can see which links may earn a commission before you follow one.
    </p>

    <h2>Buying from third parties</h2>
    <p>
      Any purchase you make is between you and the retailer. Their pricing,
      stock, delivery, returns, warranty, support and privacy practices are
      theirs, and {site.name} is not a party to the transaction and cannot
      resolve problems with an order. Their terms apply once you leave this
      site.
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</BaseLayout>
